goal: Recall what you learned without looking at your previous notes.
1. Revision checklist
Try to explain each item in one or two sentences.
Topic	What you should remember
Users	whoami, id, groups
Groups	groupadd, usermod -aG
Admin access	sudo
Services	systemctl status, start, stop, enable
Logs	journalctl, /var/log/
IP address	ip addr
Network interface	ip link
Routing	ip route
DNS	getent hosts
Connectivity	ping
Listening ports	ss -tulpen
Firewall	UFW, iptables
SSH	Default port 22

2. Draw a server troubleshooting flow
Imagine your Linux server is not accessible. Draw this flow in your notebook:
Problem: Server is not accessible

Check IP and network interface

ip addr · ip link

Check route and connectivity

ip route · ping

Check DNS and service

getent hosts · systemctl status

Check listening ports and firewall

ss -tulpen · sudo ufw status

Inspect logs and identify the issue

journalctl
